#!/usr/bin/env bash
# heimdall-presence — the dev-side client for SERVER-SYNCED TEAM PRESENCE.
#
# WHAT IT IS. A dev's hmd reports WHERE it is working (a heartbeat) to the control plane,
# and any dev can read the ONLINE team for the current project. Presence is synced
# THROUGH the server (cp_presence on the StateBackend seam — Firestore-durable on Cloud
# Run), not via local files, so a dev sees teammates on OTHER machines.
#
# SUBCOMMANDS
#   heimdall-presence beat            send a heartbeat for THIS repo's project + identity.
#   heimdall-presence roster [--json] print the ONLINE team for THIS repo's project.
#   heimdall-presence keeper-start    spawn ONE detached background beat-keeper that beats
#                                     every ~20s (under the ~45s server TTL) until the session
#                                     ends — so a LIVE-BUT-IDLE session stays on the wall even
#                                     when nothing re-renders the statusline. Idempotent (never
#                                     a second keeper for the same session/repo); consent-gated
#                                     (OFF -> no keeper); silent-safe (failures never fatal).
#   heimdall-presence keeper-stop     kill THIS session's keeper + reap its pidfile (no leak).
#
# DURABLE PRESENCE (why the keeper exists). A single SessionStart beat AGES OUT past the ~45s
# TTL on an idle-but-live session, and the statusline beat only fires when Claude Code REDRAWS
# — so a session that stops rendering silently vanishes from the wall. The keeper is a detached
# loop that re-beats on a timer (independent of renders) until keeper-stop reaps it at
# SessionEnd. It REUSES `beat` (and its consent gate) for every heartbeat — never re-implements
# beating. DEV-CHECKOUT: when heimdall is a dev checkout (on PATH, NOT a registered plugin) the
# plugin's SessionStart hook does not fire, so wire these two subcommands into your OWN
# ~/.claude/settings.json SessionStart/SessionEnd hooks (see USAGE below) — or run install.sh,
# which registers the plugin whose hooks call them for you. The runtime home + this bin are
# resolved DYNAMICALLY (never a hardcoded path), so the same wiring works on any machine.
#
# ZERO-CONFIG. A dev's FIRST beat/roster auto-resolves everything — the dev exports
# NOTHING. The CP url comes from a shipped local config, the signing key is auto-generated
# + auto-enrolled + persisted on first use, the project id is stable across clones, and the
# handle comes from heimdall-identity. Manual env overrides still win where set.
#
# IDENTITY / PROJECT / WIRE (resolved; flag > env > config/derive):
#   identity HAID : --haid > $HMD_HAID > `heimdall-identity current` (if present)
#                 > `heimdall-haid current`.
#   project       : --project > the NORMALIZED git remote (host+path, scheme/user/port
#                   stripped, .git dropped, lowercased — so every CLONE of one remote shares
#                   ONE project id) > $HMD_PROJECT > the repo dir name.
#   server URL    : --url > $HEIMDALL_CP_URL > $BASE_URL > local config
#                   ${HOME}/.heimdall/cp-endpoint.json `.url` > the SHIPPED DEFAULT
#                   (DEFAULT_CP_URL — the public surface, baked in since the URL is not a
#                   secret, so a dev sets NOTHING for the URL; only the token is distributed).
#   signing seed  : $HMD_PRESENCE_SEED (dev-scoped override, testing only) > persisted
#                   ${HOME}/.heimdall/pki/<haid>.seed (mode 0600) > AUTO-BOOTSTRAP — keygen
#                   (cp_auth), POST
#                   SECURITY: the dev signs as ITSELF with its OWN per-dev key; it MUST NOT
#                   read $HEIMDALL_CP_PKI_KEY (the SERVER's Secret-Manager identity seed —
#                   server-only, never on a dev path).
#                   {url}/enroll {haid, pubkey, handle} (the config's enroll_token rides ONLY
#                   IF configured — an OPEN server enrolls tokenless, so ZERO dev config),
#                   persist the seed 0600, reuse it thereafter. The seed lives in-process +
#                   the 0600 file ONLY — NEVER printed/logged/argv'd. A failed enroll is
#                   throttled (an mtime stamp) so it never hammers the server per render.
#   handle        : --handle > $HMD_HANDLE > `heimdall-identity --handle`.
#   beat data     : --verdict/$HMD_VERDICT, --file/$HMD_FILE.
#
# GRACEFUL DEGRADE (the statusline reads this — it MUST never traceback). With NO URL or
# NO seed, or on ANY transport/auth failure, `roster` prints a CLEAN EMPTY roster ([] for
# --json) and exits 0; `beat` is a silent no-op and exits 0. Offline is normal, not an
# error. The signing path REUSES the shipped cp_auth signer — never hand-rolled Ed25519.

set -uo pipefail

SELF_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
SELF="$SELF_DIR/heimdall-presence"   # this bin, resolved dynamically (the keeper re-invokes it for `beat`).
REPO="$(cd "$SELF_DIR/.." && pwd)"
LIB="$REPO/bin/lib"

# The SIGNED-PATH scrub. Presence carries Ed25519-signed beats AND the unsigned /enroll
# bootstrap, so a local rewriting proxy in this path is a broken signature or a compromised
# install. hmd_signed_exec drops the rewriters (HEADROOM_*, loopback proxy vars, the model
# base-URL pins) and deliberately KEEPS a corporate CONNECT proxy, which tunnels TLS and is
# often the only egress an estate has.
# shellcheck source=lib/hmd-gate-endpoint.sh
. "$LIB/hmd-gate-endpoint.sh"

# ── control-plane URL + opt-out consent (SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH) ──────────────────
# Sourced: the canonical public CP URL literal ($HEIMDALL_DEFAULT_CP_URL) + the consent
# store helpers (_cp_consent_decision / _cp_consent_url / _write_cp_consent). The gate
# below resolves the baked-in default UNLESS the dev has explicitly opted OUT — so presence
# is ON BY DEFAULT (undecided/connected phone the control plane; only a persisted DECLINE
# withholds the URL, yielding zero egress). If the lib is somehow absent, DEFAULT stays empty
# -> offline degrade (fail-safe toward silence).
# shellcheck source=lib/cp-consent.sh
[ -f "$LIB/cp-consent.sh" ] && . "$LIB/cp-consent.sh"
HAID_CLI="$SELF_DIR/heimdall-haid"
IDENTITY_CLI="$SELF_DIR/heimdall-identity"   # forward-compat: preferred when present.

PY="$(command -v python3 || command -v python || true)"

# ── parse argv (subcommand + option-style overrides) ───────────────────────────
SUB="${1:-}"; shift || true

# `doctor` delegates to the self-healing autoenroll helper (bin/heimdall-presence-doctor)
# with all remaining args (its OWN flags: --bg, --status, --once). Intercepted BEFORE this
# bin's strict option parser (which would reject --bg/--status) — exec so the doctor owns
# stdout/stderr/exit. The helper resolves the SAME interpreter/identity/project/wire this
# bin does and REUSES `beat`/`roster`/`status` for its remediation + verify.
if [ "$SUB" = "doctor" ]; then
  DOCTOR_BIN="$SELF_DIR/heimdall-presence-doctor"
  if [ -x "$DOCTOR_BIN" ]; then exec "$DOCTOR_BIN" "$@"; fi
  echo "heimdall-presence: doctor helper not found or not executable ($DOCTOR_BIN)" >&2
  exit 2
fi
HAID=""; PROJECT=""; URL=""; HANDLE=""; VERDICT=""; FILE=""; JSON=""; GLOBAL=""; NOFILES=""
# Keeper-scoped overrides. SESSION keys the per-session pidfile so the SessionEnd stop reaps
# EXACTLY the keeper this session's SessionStart spawned (never a teammate's live session).
# It may legitimately be EMPTY (a hook passing an absent session_id) — so it is NOT `:?`-guarded.
SESSION=""; INTERVAL=""; KEEPER_PIDFILE=""
# STRICT surfaces a DROPPED/refused beat LOUDLY (nonzero exit) instead of the fire-and-forget
# exit-0 the statusline relies on. Default is the silent-safe path; --strict / HMD_PRESENCE_STRICT=1
# opts in (used by tooling + the BUG2 regression test to prove a failed beat no longer fakes
# success). Either way a dropped beat is NAMED on stderr (below) so a human running it manually
# — the exact way the invisible-beat bug surfaced — sees the failure instead of nothing.
STRICT="${HMD_PRESENCE_STRICT:-}"
while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
  case "$1" in
    --haid)    HAID="${2:?--haid needs a value}"; shift 2 ;;
    --project) PROJECT="${2:?--project needs a value}"; shift 2 ;;
    --url)     URL="${2:?--url needs a value}"; shift 2 ;;
    --handle)  HANDLE="${2:?--handle needs a value}"; shift 2 ;;
    --verdict) VERDICT="${2:?--verdict needs a value}"; shift 2 ;;
    --file)    FILE="${2:?--file needs a value}"; shift 2 ;;
    --json)    JSON="1"; shift ;;
    --global)  GLOBAL="1"; shift ;;   # off/on: machine-wide kill switch (~/.heimdall/presence-off)
    --no-files) NOFILES="1"; shift ;; # on: stay present but withhold file/activity detail
    --strict)  STRICT="1"; shift ;;   # beat: surface a dropped/refused beat with a nonzero exit
    --session)  SESSION="${2-}"; shift 2 ;;   # keeper: per-session pidfile key (may be empty)
    --interval) INTERVAL="${2-}"; shift 2 ;;  # keeper: beat period in seconds (default 20)
    --pidfile)  KEEPER_PIDFILE="${2-}"; shift 2 ;;  # keeper: explicit pidfile (test seam)
    *) echo "heimdall-presence: unexpected argument: $1" >&2; exit 2 ;;
  esac
done

# INTERACTIVE gates the LOUD, actionable crypto-missing warning (below) to a HUMAN who ran
# `heimdall-presence beat` at a terminal. The statusline/keeper fork beats with stderr
# redirected to /dev/null (NOT a tty), so `[ -t 2 ]` is False there → they stay SILENT
# (no spam, exit 0 — the strict silent-safe contract the statusline relies on). An explicit
# HMD_PRESENCE_INTERACTIVE=1 forces it on for tooling/tests that cannot allocate a pty. This
# is the interactive-vs-render distinction the crypto-gap warning hooks onto.
INTERACTIVE=""
if [ -n "${HMD_PRESENCE_INTERACTIVE:-}" ] || [ -t 2 ]; then INTERACTIVE="1"; fi

# `roster --json` with nothing configured must STILL emit a clean empty roster — define
# the offline emitters up front so every degrade path is one call (no traceback, exit 0).
emit_empty_roster() {
  if [ -n "$JSON" ]; then printf '[]\n'; else printf 'presence: no teammates online\n'; fi
  exit 0
}
beat_noop() { exit 0; }   # an unconfigured/failed beat is a silent no-op (offline is fine).

# Probe the Ed25519 signing backend for `status` — the natural place a dev checks WHY presence
# is not working. Prints "ok:<backend>" (cp_auth.crypto_available() True), "missing" (degraded
# mode — no seed can mint, the dev is invisible), or "unknown" (cannot probe). Read-only; never
# raises. Distinct from the OFF/consent state — a dev can be ON yet invisible due to this gap.
_signing_probe() {
  { [ -n "$PY" ] && [ -f "$LIB/cp_auth.py" ]; } || { printf 'unknown'; return; }
  LIB="$LIB" "$PY" - <<'PYEOF' 2>/dev/null
import os, sys
sys.path.insert(0, os.environ["LIB"])
try:
    import cp_auth as K
    if K.crypto_available():
        sys.stdout.write("ok:" + (K.backend_name() or "ed25519"))
    else:
        sys.stdout.write("missing")
except Exception:
    sys.stdout.write("unknown")
PYEOF
}

# The activity verbs bump/read a LOCAL mtime stamp (bash + stat only, no python, no wire), so
# they must NOT be swallowed by the no-python / no-crypto degrade the wire verbs need.
if [ "$SUB" != "activity" ] && [ "$SUB" != "activity-ts" ]; then
  [ -n "$PY" ] || { [ "$SUB" = "roster" ] && emit_empty_roster || beat_noop; }
  [ -f "$LIB/cp_auth.py" ] || { [ "$SUB" = "roster" ] && emit_empty_roster || beat_noop; }
fi

# ── local config (${HOME}/.heimdall/cp-endpoint.json) — the shipped CP endpoint ──
# Zero-config: the install ships {url, enroll_token} here so a dev exports NOTHING. Parsed
# via python (already required above) so there is no jq dependency on the degrade path.
HMD_DIR="${HOME:-}/.heimdall"
CONFIG_FILE="$HMD_DIR/cp-endpoint.json"
CFG_URL=""; CFG_TOKEN=""
if [ -n "${HOME:-}" ] && [ -f "$CONFIG_FILE" ]; then
  CFG_OUT="$("$PY" - "$CONFIG_FILE" 2>/dev/null <<'PYEOF' || true
import json, sys
try:
    d = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))
    sys.stdout.write((d.get("url") or "") + "\n" + (d.get("enroll_token") or "") + "\n")
except Exception:
    sys.stdout.write("\n\n")
PYEOF
)"
  CFG_URL="$(printf '%s\n' "$CFG_OUT" | sed -n '1p')"
  CFG_TOKEN="$(printf '%s\n' "$CFG_OUT" | sed -n '2p')"
fi

# ── PRESENCE OPT-OUT (consent surface) — per-repo + global toggles ───────────────
# State (local, cheap, readable — no server round-trip to CHECK it):
#   • per-repo: <repo>/.heimdall/presence.json -> {"enabled": false} silences THIS repo;
#     {"files": false} keeps the dev present but withholds file detail. (gitignored by
#     `.heimdall/*` — one dev's choice must NEVER commit into a teammate's repo.)
#   • global:  ~/.heimdall/presence-off (EXISTENCE = off), mirroring the no-autoupdate stamp.
# EFFECTIVE = NOT global-off AND NOT repo-off. Default (no files) = ON — existing users
# unchanged. OFF = invisible (no beats), NOT blind (roster/status still work).
GLOBAL_OFF_FILE="$HMD_DIR/presence-off"
_pres_state_dir() {
  if [ -n "${HEIMDALL_PRESENCE_DIR:-}" ]; then printf '%s' "$HEIMDALL_PRESENCE_DIR"; return; fi
  local top; top="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || true)"
  if [ -n "$top" ]; then printf '%s/.heimdall' "$top"; else printf '%s/.heimdall' "$PWD"; fi
}
PRES_STATE_DIR="$(_pres_state_dir)"
PRES_STATE_FILE="$PRES_STATE_DIR/presence.json"

# Effective-state probes are PURE BASH ($(<file) is a builtin — no python, no subprocess),
# so a `beat` no-op is a stat-only fast path a cron/hook can't leak around the toggle.
_global_pres_off() { [ -f "$GLOBAL_OFF_FILE" ]; }
_repo_pres_off() {
  [ -f "$PRES_STATE_FILE" ] || return 1
  local c; c="$(<"$PRES_STATE_FILE")" 2>/dev/null || return 1
  [[ "$c" =~ \"enabled\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*false ]]
}
_pres_off() { _global_pres_off || _repo_pres_off; }
_repo_nofiles() {   # the --no-files sub-toggle: present, but file detail withheld.
  [ -f "$PRES_STATE_FILE" ] || return 1
  local c; c="$(<"$PRES_STATE_FILE")" 2>/dev/null || return 1
  [[ "$c" =~ \"files\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*false ]]
}
_write_pres_state() {   # atomic write of presence.json (gitignored; non-secret).
  mkdir -p "$PRES_STATE_DIR" 2>/dev/null || true
  local tmp="$PRES_STATE_FILE.tmp.$$"
  printf '%s\n' "$1" > "$tmp" 2>/dev/null && mv -f "$tmp" "$PRES_STATE_FILE" 2>/dev/null
}

# The one-time opt-in HINT throttle. When the dev is UNDECIDED and we cannot prompt (a
# non-interactive hook/CLI), `connect-prompt` prints ONE line pointing at `hmd presence
# connect` — but at most once per window (an mtime stamp, like the crypto-warn throttle) so
# a per-session SessionStart hook never nags. Returns 0 (print now, and bump the stamp) when
# the stamp is absent or older than the window; 1 (stay silent) otherwise. Never persists a
# decision — undecided stays undecided so a later interactive session can still prompt.
_cp_hint_throttled() {
  local st="${HMD_CP_HINT_STAMP:-$HMD_DIR/.cp-hint-stamp}" now mt window="${HMD_CP_HINT_WINDOW:-72000}"
  now="$(date +%s 2>/dev/null || echo 0)"
  mt="$(_stamp_mtime "$st")"
  if [ -n "$mt" ] && [ "$(( now - mt ))" -lt "$window" ]; then return 1; fi
  mkdir -p "$(dirname "$st")" 2>/dev/null || true
  : > "$st" 2>/dev/null || true
  return 0
}

# ── ACTIVITY STAMP (the wall-state ACTIVE/IDLE signal) ─────────────────────────────
# A local mtime stamp under the per-repo state dir marks the LAST time this dev did REAL WORK
# (an edit, or an active gate verdict). `beat` sends its mtime as the body's `activity_ts`, so
# the server DERIVES ACTIVE (activity fresh) vs IDLE (activity stale/absent) — an idle beater
# stays on the wall, demoted not dropped. It is CLIENT-OWNED and LOCAL: a pure mtime, no network,
# no secret, scoped to THIS repo/dev. TWO bump paths (the plan's "edit hook + verdict"):
#   • the edit hook (PostToolUse) shells `heimdall-presence activity` after a write, and
#   • an ACTIVE-verdict beat (working/pass/deny/scanning, NOT watching/idle) bumps it inline.
# A bare keeper/daemon beat (no verdict) does NOT bump — it only READS the stamp forward, so a
# dev who stopped working decays ACTIVE -> IDLE across the activity window, then OFFLINE when the
# beats stop. HMD_ACTIVITY_STAMP overrides the path (tests); HMD_ACTIVITY_TS overrides the value.
_activity_stamp_path() { printf '%s' "${HMD_ACTIVITY_STAMP:-$PRES_STATE_DIR/.activity-stamp}"; }
_bump_activity_stamp() {
  local st; st="$(_activity_stamp_path)"
  mkdir -p "$(dirname "$st")" 2>/dev/null || true
  : > "$st" 2>/dev/null || true
}
# epoch-seconds mtime of $1 (macOS `stat -f %m` / GNU `stat -c %Y`); empty if absent.
_stamp_mtime() { [ -f "$1" ] || return 0; stat -f %m "$1" 2>/dev/null || stat -c %Y "$1" 2>/dev/null || true; }
# The activity_ts the NEXT beat will send: HMD_ACTIVITY_TS override > now (bumping the stamp)
# when this beat carries an ACTIVE verdict > the existing stamp mtime (carried forward by a bare
# keeper/daemon beat) > empty (no known activity -> the server derives IDLE). Printed by the
# `activity-ts` verb (a debug/test seam) and consumed inline by the `beat` case.
_resolve_activity_ts() {
  if [ -n "${HMD_ACTIVITY_TS:-}" ]; then printf '%s' "$HMD_ACTIVITY_TS"; return; fi
  case "$VERDICT" in
    ""|watching|idle|IDLE|Watching|WATCHING) : ;;   # empty / idle sentinel -> not an active signal
    *) _bump_activity_stamp ;;                        # real work this beat -> bump the stamp to now
  esac
  local mt; mt="$(_stamp_mtime "$(_activity_stamp_path)")"
  [ -n "$mt" ] && printf '%s' "$mt"
}

# The repo-relative git BRANCH this beat rides (so teammates' statuslines can show a same-repo
# dev who is off on ANOTHER branch, with their branch under their name). HMD_BRANCH overrides
# (tests); else `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`. A detached HEAD (bare "HEAD") degrades to the
# short sha so the render still marks "off on a commit", never the literal word HEAD. Empty
# outside any git repo (the render then shows no branch line). Pure git read, no network.
_resolve_branch() {
  if [ -n "${HMD_BRANCH:-}" ]; then printf '%s' "$HMD_BRANCH"; return; fi
  local b; b="$(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD 2>/dev/null || true)"
  if [ "$b" = "HEAD" ]; then b="$(git rev-parse --short HEAD 2>/dev/null || true)"; fi
  [ -n "$b" ] && printf '%s' "$b"
}

# OFF = ZERO beats. A `beat` (from the statusline fork, a cron, or a hook) is a stat-only
# no-op when effectively off — no python, no network, no seed bootstrap. This is defense in
# depth: the statusline also skips the beat when off, but the toggle is enforced HERE too so
# nothing can leak a beat around it. Retire/roster/status/on/off still run when off.
if [ "$SUB" = "beat" ] && _pres_off; then beat_noop; fi

# Normalize a git remote URL to a STABLE project id: host+path, with scheme/userinfo/port
# stripped, an scp-style "host:path" colon -> "/", a trailing .git dropped, lowercased. All
# clones of one remote (https or ssh, any user/port) collapse to ONE id, so teammates on
# other machines/clones land in the SAME project.
normalize_remote() {
  printf '%s' "$1" \
    | sed -e 's#^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*://##' \
          -e 's#^[^@/]*@##' \
          -e 's#:[0-9][0-9]*/#/#' \
          -e 's#:#/#' \
          -e 's#\.git$##' \
          -e 's#/$##' \
    | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]'
}

# ── resolve identity / project / wire (flag > env > config/derive) ─────────────
[ -n "$HAID" ] || HAID="${HMD_HAID:-}"
if [ -z "$HAID" ]; then
  if [ -x "$IDENTITY_CLI" ]; then HAID="$("$IDENTITY_CLI" current 2>/dev/null || true)"; fi
fi
if [ -z "$HAID" ] && [ -x "$HAID_CLI" ]; then
  HAID="$("$HAID_CLI" current 2>/dev/null || true)"
fi

# project = STABLE across clones: --project flag wins; else the NORMALIZED git remote (so
# every clone of one remote shares ONE id, putting teammates in the SAME project); else
# $HMD_PROJECT; else the working tree's top-level dir name. Derived from CWD so the project
# tracks the repo the dev is in (not the heimdall checkout that hosts this script).
if [ -z "$PROJECT" ]; then
  REMOTE_URL="$(git config --get remote.origin.url 2>/dev/null || true)"
  [ -n "$REMOTE_URL" ] && PROJECT="$(normalize_remote "$REMOTE_URL")"
  [ -n "$PROJECT" ] || PROJECT="${HMD_PROJECT:-}"
  if [ -z "$PROJECT" ]; then
    TOP="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || true)"
    [ -n "$TOP" ] && PROJECT="$(basename "$TOP")"
  fi
fi

# DISPLAY LABEL (§3) — a human-readable name for the roster/statusline render. This does NOT change
# PROJECT (the partition key — stable across clones, must stay the normalized remote). For a github
# repo the label is the owner/name slug (drop the `github.com/` prefix) — never a bare working-tree
# dir name like `code`/`Downloads` leaking from the basename fallback; for a non-github remote the
# normalized PROJECT stands; for a truly-local tree the tree's basename is the best we have.
if [ -z "${PROJECT_LABEL:-}" ]; then
  case "$PROJECT" in
    github.com/*/*) PROJECT_LABEL="${PROJECT#github.com/}" ;;   # -> owner/name
    *)              PROJECT_LABEL="$PROJECT" ;;
  esac
fi

[ -n "$URL" ] || URL="${HEIMDALL_CP_URL:-${BASE_URL:-}}"
[ -n "$URL" ] || URL="$CFG_URL"
# Canonical public-surface URL (sourced from lib/cp-consent.sh — the ONE place the literal
# lives). NOT a secret (a public --allow-unauthenticated Cloud Run endpoint). It is the
# value `connect` persists and the value the opt-OUT gate resolves by DEFAULT (unless severed).
DEFAULT_CP_URL="${HEIMDALL_DEFAULT_CP_URL:-}"
# OPT-OUT GATE (DEFAULT ON): the baked-in public CP is resolved for the ZERO-config default
# path UNLESS the dev has EXPLICITLY opted out (persisted {"decision":"severed"} — or the legacy
# {"decision":"declined"} from the old `disconnect` name — in ~/.heimdall/cp-consent.json).
# Undecided => ON (auto-connect); connected => ON (stored/default url); SEVERED/declined => URL
# stays EMPTY => presence degrades to LOCAL/offline (empty roster, no-op beat, NO enroll) below
# => ZERO network egress. That empty-URL degrade (a few lines down) IS the privacy guarantee:
# sever and NOTHING leaves this machine. An explicit --url / $HEIMDALL_CP_URL / $BASE_URL /
# cp-endpoint.json already won above.
_CP_DECISION="$(_cp_consent_decision 2>/dev/null)"
if [ -z "$URL" ] && [ "$_CP_DECISION" != "severed" ] && [ "$_CP_DECISION" != "declined" ]; then
  URL="$(_cp_consent_url 2>/dev/null)"
fi
ENROLL_TOKEN="$CFG_TOKEN"   # the bootstrap enroll credential (config-only; never derived).
SEED="${HMD_PRESENCE_SEED:-}"   # dev-scoped override only; NEVER the server's $HEIMDALL_CP_PKI_KEY
[ -n "$HANDLE" ]  || HANDLE="${HMD_HANDLE:-}"
if [ -z "$HANDLE" ] && [ -x "$IDENTITY_CLI" ]; then
  HANDLE="$("$IDENTITY_CLI" --handle 2>/dev/null || true)"
fi
[ -n "$VERDICT" ] || VERDICT="${HMD_VERDICT:-}"
[ -n "$FILE" ]    || FILE="${HMD_FILE:-}"

# Per-(machine,repo) seed + enroll-throttle paths, keyed by haid (slugged so ':' and '/'
# never break the filename). The seed material lives ONLY in this 0600 file + the signing
# process — the bash side handles the PATH, never the seed bytes.
PKI_DIR=""; SEED_FILE=""; ENROLL_STAMP=""; CRYPTO_WARN_STAMP=""; DOCTOR_DIAG=""
if [ -n "${HOME:-}" ] && [ -n "$HAID" ]; then
  PKI_DIR="$HMD_DIR/pki"
  HAID_SLUG="$(printf '%s' "$HAID" | tr '/:' '__')"
  SEED_FILE="$PKI_DIR/$HAID_SLUG.seed"
  ENROLL_STAMP="$PKI_DIR/$HAID_SLUG.enroll-attempt"
  # The self-heal doctor's persisted last-diagnosis (heimdall-presence-doctor writes it; the
  # status subcommand below surfaces it so a dev sees WHY presence is/isn't healthy).
  DOCTOR_DIAG="$PKI_DIR/$HAID_SLUG.doctor-diagnosis"
  # A DEDICATED once-per-window mtime stamp for the crypto-missing warning — separate from
  # the enroll-attempt stamp (which crypto-missing never reaches, since keygen fails first)
  # so the loud warning throttles to ONE line per window without perturbing enroll backoff.
  CRYPTO_WARN_STAMP="$PKI_DIR/$HAID_SLUG.crypto-warn"
fi

# OFFLINE / UNCONFIGURED -> clean degrade. We need a URL, an identity, and a project; the
# SEED may legitimately be ABSENT here — the client auto-bootstraps it in-process below
# (persisted 0600 seed, else keygen+enroll). With no URL/identity/project there is nothing
# to do. The statusline relies on this: presence is a best-effort overlay, never a hard dep.
if [ -z "$URL" ] || [ -z "$HAID" ] || [ -z "$PROJECT" ]; then
  case "$SUB" in
    roster) emit_empty_roster ;;
    beat)   beat_noop ;;
  esac
fi

# ── per-repo TEAM secret (multi-tenant presence) — ONE CANONICAL FILE ───────────
# The team secret lives PER-REPO in <repo>/.heimdall/team.json — the SINGLE canonical
# file every reader (this client, heimdall-team, heimdall-invite) resolves from, NOT
# the global cp-endpoint.json (a dev may be on different teams in different repos).
# In a PRIVATE repo team.json is TRACKED/committed (so a teammate who clones the repo
# ALREADY HAS it -> auto-joins with zero commands); in a PUBLIC repo it is gitignored
# (grown via `hmd invite`). It is sent ONCE in the X-Heimdall-Team-Secret header at
# /enroll; signed beats/reads thereafter carry NO secret (membership is server-side —
# the signed GET /roster returns the caller's team). If team.json is ABSENT the FIRST
# RUN resolves the team at WIRE TIME (_resolve_team_for_wire, just before enroll/beat):
# a GitHub repo + `gh` auto-forms the repo's shared team via POST /team/auto (zero-touch —
# the first teammate INITIATES it, everyone else AUTO-JOINS, no invite/paste; the returned
# team_id is persisted with NO bearer secret, source:"auto-github"); everything else
# (no gh / no GitHub remote / air-gapped) falls back to a SILENT solo-mint so a dev is
# still ZERO-CONFIG in their OWN solo team. A legacy team.shared.json (the old two-file
# model's committed secret) is STILL READ for back-compat. The secret crosses bash->python
# via the ENVIRONMENT only — NEVER argv (argv shows in `ps`). THIS block only READS an
# existing binding; the mint/auto-github decision is deferred to the wire verb below.
TEAM_DIR="${HEIMDALL_TEAM_DIR:-}"
if [ -z "$TEAM_DIR" ]; then
  TEAM_TOP="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || true)"
  if [ -n "$TEAM_TOP" ]; then TEAM_DIR="$TEAM_TOP/.heimdall"; else TEAM_DIR="$PWD/.heimdall"; fi
fi
TEAM_FILE="$TEAM_DIR/team.json"
SHARED_FILE="$TEAM_DIR/team.shared.json"   # LEGACY committed secret (read-only back-compat)
TEAM_SECRET=""
# READ the team secret — precedence IDENTICAL to heimdall-team `_resolve` so both readers
# agree byte-for-byte: an EXPLICIT team.json (source new|join|rotate — a deliberate mint/join,
# incl. the committed private-repo team) wins; else the legacy committed team.shared.json (a
# teammate who cloned an OLD repo auto-joins); else an auto-solo/legacy team.json. READ-ONLY:
# a VIRGIN checkout (no binding yet) leaves TEAM_SECRET EMPTY here — the first-run mint (zero-
# touch auto-github, else solo) happens at WIRE TIME in _resolve_team_for_wire, so an existing
# binding short-circuits and a GitHub repo gets the auto-team path before any solo-mint. All IO
# is python-side (no jq dependency); any failure leaves TEAM_SECRET empty (graceful, never a
# traceback). An AUTO-GITHUB team.json carries a team_id + NO team_secret -> empty here (correct:
# membership is server-side, no header rides).
TEAM_SECRET="$(HMD_TEAM_FILE_R="$TEAM_FILE" HMD_TEAM_SHARED_R="$SHARED_FILE" "$PY" - 2>/dev/null <<'PYEOF' || true
import json, os, sys
path = os.environ["HMD_TEAM_FILE_R"]
shared = os.environ["HMD_TEAM_SHARED_R"]

def _read(p):
    """(secret, source) from a team file, ("","") if absent/unreadable."""
    try:
        d = json.load(open(p))
        s = d.get("team_secret")
    except Exception:
        return "", ""
    if isinstance(s, str) and s:
        src = d.get("source")
        return s, (src if isinstance(src, str) else "")
    return "", ""

def _team_id(p):
    """The stored server team_id (github binding), else "" — absent/unreadable is "" too."""
    try:
        t = json.load(open(p)).get("team_id")
    except Exception:
        return ""
    return t if isinstance(t, str) and t else ""

# P1 — a GITHUB BINDING: team.json carries a server team_id (source:auto-github, OR a MIGRATED
# committed file that ALSO kept its bearer secret for the offline fallback). Membership IS the
# server repo->team binding, so send NO header even when a committed secret coexists — a secret
# header would re-bind this HAID to sha256(secret) and re-SPLIT the repo (the team-split bug).
if _team_id(path):
    sys.stdout.write(""); sys.exit(0)
ps, psrc = _read(path)
ss, _ss = _read(shared)
# 1) a DELIBERATE team.json (new|join|rotate) wins — incl. the committed private team.
if ps and psrc in ("new", "join", "rotate"):
    sys.stdout.write(ps); sys.exit(0)
# 2) the LEGACY committed team.shared.json (back-compat auto-join).
if ss:
    sys.stdout.write(ss); sys.exit(0)
# 3) an auto-solo / legacy team.json (a secret-bearing binding).
if ps:
    sys.stdout.write(ps); sys.exit(0)
# 4) FIRST RUN (no binding yet, or an auto-github team.json with no secret): stay EMPTY.
#    _resolve_team_for_wire mints/auto-joins right before enroll/beat.
sys.stdout.write("")
PYEOF
)"

# ── the signed HTTP client (REUSE the shipped cp_auth signer over urllib) ──────
# The seed is resolved IN-PROCESS (env > the 0600 seed file > auto-bootstrap) and is NEVER
# argv'd (argv shows in `ps`) or printed — only the seed-file PATH crosses from bash. POST
# /presence carries the heartbeat body; GET /roster?project=<p> is the GFE-safe read
# (job_id-style: project in the QUERY, EMPTY body — Google's GFE rejects a GET-with-a-body).
# The signature covers the FULL path-with-query (canonical_message), so the read is
# authenticated + tamper-evident. Mirrors deploy/cloud-run remote_client.py.
run_client() {
  LIB="$LIB" PRES_URL="$URL" PRES_HAID="$HAID" PRES_SEED="$SEED" \
  PRES_SEED_FILE="$SEED_FILE" PRES_ENROLL_TOKEN="$ENROLL_TOKEN" \
  PRES_ENROLL_STAMP="$ENROLL_STAMP" PRES_THROTTLE="${HMD_ENROLL_THROTTLE:-180}" \
  PRES_PROJECT="$PROJECT" PRES_PROJECT_LABEL="${PROJECT_LABEL:-$PROJECT}" PRES_HANDLE="$HANDLE" PRES_VERDICT="$VERDICT" \
  PRES_FILE="$FILE" PRES_VERB="$1" PRES_JSON="$JSON" PRES_TEAM_SECRET="$TEAM_SECRET" \
  PRES_ACTIVITY_TS="${ACTIVITY_TS:-}" PRES_BRANCH="${BRANCH:-}" \
  PRES_STRICT="$STRICT" PRES_INTERACTIVE="$INTERACTIVE" \
  PRES_CRYPTO_WARN_STAMP="$CRYPTO_WARN_STAMP" \
  PRES_GH_USER="${PRES_GH_USER:-}" PRES_GH_PROOF="${PRES_GH_PROOF:-}" PRES_REPO="${PRES_REPO:-}" \
  hmd_signed_exec "$PY" - <<'PYEOF'
import contextlib
import json
import os
import secrets
import sys
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

sys.path.insert(0, os.environ["LIB"])
import cp_auth as K  # the SHIPPED Ed25519 signer + keygen — never re-implemented.

BASE = os.environ["PRES_URL"].rstrip("/")
HAID = os.environ["PRES_HAID"]
VERB = os.environ["PRES_VERB"]
AS_JSON = bool(os.environ.get("PRES_JSON"))


def request(method, path, body, seed, *, timeout=10):
    """Sign canonical_message(METHOD, PATH, BODY) with `seed` and drive an HTTPS request.
    `path` is the FULL path AS TRANSMITTED (incl. any ?query — the signature covers it).
    An EMPTY body is sent as a TRUE bodyless request (data=None) so a GFE-safe GET carries
    no body. Returns (status, parsed_dict); a transport error returns (0, {})."""
    if isinstance(body, str):
        body = body.encode("utf-8")
    data = body if body else None
    req = urllib.request.Request(BASE + path, data=data, method=method)
    req.add_header("X-Heimdall-HAID", HAID)
    if data is not None:
        req.add_header("Content-Type", "application/json")
    req.add_header("X-Heimdall-Signature", K.sign(seed, K.canonical_message(method, path, body)))
    # The per-repo TEAM SECRET rides the header on EVERY presence call (beat / retire / roster),
    # not just enroll — the server hashes it (derive_team_id) to the SAME partition the browser
    # /roster-team read derives, so a signed beat lands EXACTLY where its team.json secret reads it
    # back (the BUG2 write<->read round-trip). The signature covers only method+path+body, so this
    # header never perturbs it; the secret is sent over TLS, never argv, never logged.
    team_secret = os.environ.get("PRES_TEAM_SECRET") or ""
    if team_secret:
        req.add_header("X-Heimdall-Team-Secret", team_secret)
    token = os.environ.get("ID_TOKEN") or ""   # optional Cloud Run IAM bearer.
    if token:
        req.add_header("Authorization", "Bearer " + token)
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:
            raw = resp.read()
            return resp.status, (json.loads(raw) if raw else {})
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        raw = exc.read()
        try:
            return exc.code, (json.loads(raw) if raw else {})
        except (ValueError, TypeError):
            return exc.code, {}
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — any transport/TLS/DNS fault degrades to offline.
        return 0, {}


# ── seed resolution + auto-bootstrap (zero-config: keygen -> enroll -> persist) ──


def _enroll(body, token, *, timeout=10):
    """The bootstrap enroll: POST /enroll {haid, pubkey, handle}. UNSIGNED by design — this
    is the chicken-and-egg step that REGISTERS the key, so no signature exists yet. The
    config's enroll_token rides in X-Heimdall-Enroll-Token ONLY WHEN ONE IS CONFIGURED; an
    OPEN server (HEIMDALL_ENROLL_OPEN=1) accepts a tokenless enroll, so a token is OMITTED
    when absent (a token-mode server still gets it). Returns the HTTP status (0 on any
    transport error).

    MULTI-TENANT: the per-repo TEAM SECRET (PRES_TEAM_SECRET, from <repo>/.heimdall/
    team.json — auto-minted if absent) rides the X-Heimdall-Team-Secret HEADER (kept
    out of any body log). The server hashes it to a team_id, binds this HAID to that
    team, and DISCARDS the raw secret — it is sent ONCE here at enroll; signed beats/
    reads thereafter carry NO secret (membership is server-side). Omitted when empty
    (a single-tenant/back-compat server maps an absent secret to its default team)."""
    req = urllib.request.Request(BASE + "/enroll", data=body, method="POST")
    req.add_header("Content-Type", "application/json")
    req.add_header("X-Heimdall-HAID", HAID)
    if token:
        req.add_header("X-Heimdall-Enroll-Token", token)
    team_secret = os.environ.get("PRES_TEAM_SECRET") or ""
    if team_secret:
        req.add_header("X-Heimdall-Team-Secret", team_secret)
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:
            resp.read()
            return resp.status
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        return exc.code
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — offline / DNS / TLS -> a failed enroll.
        return 0


def _persisted_seed():
    """The base64 seed from the per-(machine,repo) 0600 file, or '' if absent/unreadable.
    Read here so the seed material stays in this process + the file ONLY (never bash/argv)."""
    path = os.environ.get("PRES_SEED_FILE") or ""
    if not path or not os.path.exists(path):
        return ""
    try:
        with open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            return fh.read().strip()
    except OSError:
        return ""


def _warn_crypto_missing():
    """Emit ONE actionable stderr line when the Ed25519 signing backend is missing — the
    PERSISTENT, actionable misconfig that silently made a dev INVISIBLE (keygen raises
    AuthError('crypto_unavailable'), the seed is never minted, every beat is dropped
    unsigned, and nothing surfaced why — the bug that cost hours). The line names the ACTUAL
    interpreter (sys.executable) + the exact pip fix so the human can act immediately.

    GATED to PRES_INTERACTIVE (a human at a terminal, or an explicit opt-in) — the statusline
    /keeper render fork runs it with PRES_INTERACTIVE unset, so it stays SILENT + exit 0 (the
    strict silent-safe contract; the statusline must never spam or traceback). THROTTLED by an
    mtime stamp (PRES_CRYPTO_WARN_STAMP, same window as the enroll throttle) so an interactive
    beat loop prints it ONCE per window, not every beat. stdout is NEVER touched (the statusline
    reads stdout)."""
    if not os.environ.get("PRES_INTERACTIVE"):
        return
    stamp = os.environ.get("PRES_CRYPTO_WARN_STAMP") or ""
    throttle = float(os.environ.get("PRES_THROTTLE") or "180")
    now = time.time()
    # Back off if we warned recently — one loud line per window, never a per-beat spew.
    if stamp and os.path.exists(stamp):
        recent = False
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            recent = (now - os.path.getmtime(stamp)) < throttle
        if recent:
            return
    if stamp:
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(stamp), mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
            with open(stamp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                fh.write("%f" % now)
    py = sys.executable or "python3"
    sys.stderr.write(
        "heimdall presence: signing backend missing (Ed25519) — you are INVISIBLE to your "
        "team. fix: %s -m pip install --user cryptography\n" % py)


def _bootstrap_seed():
    """Auto-enroll once: keygen (cp_auth) -> POST /enroll -> persist the seed 0600 -> return
    it. Throttled by an mtime stamp so a FAILING enroll does NOT hammer the server every
    render. Silent + non-fatal: ANY failure returns '' (the caller degrades to offline). Runs
    at most once — a later render finds the persisted seed and skips this.

    TOKEN-OPTIONAL: bootstrap proceeds whenever there is a URL (always — a shipped default)
    and a place to persist the seed. The enroll token is sent ONLY IF configured, so an OPEN
    server (HEIMDALL_ENROLL_OPEN=1) auto-enrolls a dev with ZERO config; a token-mode server
    still works because a configured token is still sent."""
    # CRYPTO-MISSING is a DISTINCT failure from transient offline/DNS/TLS: the Ed25519 backend
    # is absent (cp_auth.crypto_available() is False), so keygen can NEVER succeed and NO seed
    # will EVER mint — a PERSISTENT, actionable misconfig, not a network blip. Surface it LOUD
    # (interactive beat only, throttled) instead of the silent '' that hid the invisible-beat
    # bug; the statusline/keeper render fork stays muted (PRES_INTERACTIVE unset). Checked FIRST,
    # before the enroll throttle/network, because it is settled without any request.
    if not K.crypto_available():
        if VERB == "beat":
            _warn_crypto_missing()
        return ""
    token = os.environ.get("PRES_ENROLL_TOKEN") or ""
    seed_file = os.environ.get("PRES_SEED_FILE") or ""
    if not BASE or not seed_file:
        return ""   # no URL / nowhere to persist the seed -> stay offline.
    stamp = os.environ.get("PRES_ENROLL_STAMP") or ""
    throttle = float(os.environ.get("PRES_THROTTLE") or "180")
    now = time.time()
    # Back off if we attempted recently — a failed enroll must not retry every render.
    if stamp and os.path.exists(stamp):
        recent = False
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            recent = (now - os.path.getmtime(stamp)) < throttle
        if recent:
            return ""
    try:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(seed_file), mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    except OSError:
        return ""
    # Stamp the attempt BEFORE the network call so a crash/failure still throttles.
    if stamp:
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError), open(stamp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write("%f" % now)
    try:
        priv_b64, pub_b64 = K.generate_keypair()  # REUSE — never hand-roll Ed25519.
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — crypto unavailable / keygen fault -> offline.
        return ""
    body = json.dumps({
        "haid": HAID,
        "pubkey": pub_b64,
        "handle": os.environ.get("PRES_HANDLE") or None,
    }).encode("utf-8")
    status = _enroll(body, token)
    if not 200 <= status < 300:
        # LOUD on a REFUSED *CONFIGURED* enroll, mute otherwise. A 4xx means a reachable
        # server ACTIVELY REFUSED this enroll — but that is only a CREDENTIAL error worth
        # surfacing when the dev actually configured a token (a wrong/expired/revoked
        # enroll_token). A wrong token must NOT look like success, so name it ONCE on
        # stderr (the throttle stamp keeps it to one line per window). Everything else
        # stays MUTE: a tokenless zero-config beat merely probing the shipped DEFAULT
        # endpoint (no token, no expressed intent) gets a 4xx as a matter of course —
        # that is the beat's silent-no-op contract, not a credential error — and a
        # transport failure (status 0 == offline/DNS/TLS) or a 5xx (transient server
        # fault) are never credential errors either.
        if token and 400 <= status < 500:
            sys.stderr.write(
                "heimdall enroll refused (%d): check the enroll token / endpoint\n"
                % status)
        return ""   # enroll refused/offline -> no seed (the stamp throttles the retry).
    # Persist the seed 0600 (created restrictively; never world/group-readable).
    try:
        fd = os.open(seed_file, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
        try:
            os.write(fd, priv_b64.encode("ascii"))
        finally:
            os.close(fd)
        os.chmod(seed_file, 0o600)
    except OSError:
        return ""
    return priv_b64


def resolve_seed():
    """The signing seed: $HMD_PRESENCE_SEED (PRES_SEED — dev-scoped override) > the
    persisted 0600 seed > AUTO-BOOTSTRAP (keygen + enroll + persist). '' -> offline.
    NEVER the server's $HEIMDALL_CP_PKI_KEY (Secret-Manager identity, server-only)."""
    env_seed = os.environ.get("PRES_SEED") or ""
    if env_seed:
        return env_seed
    persisted = _persisted_seed()
    if persisted:
        return persisted
    return _bootstrap_seed()


def render_roster(rows):
    """Print the online team. --json -> the raw roster list; else one line per dev:
    <handle-or-haid>  <verdict>  <file>  (<age>s ago)."""
    if AS_JSON:
        sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(rows, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
        return
    if not rows:
        sys.stdout.write("presence: no teammates online\n")
        return
    # A one-line context header naming the repo by its human LABEL (owner/name for a github repo),
    # not the raw partition key or a bare dir name. Only when there ARE teammates, so the ubiquitous
    # empty-roster line is byte-identical.
    label = os.environ.get("PRES_PROJECT_LABEL") or os.environ.get("PRES_PROJECT") or ""
    if label:
        sys.stdout.write("presence: %s\n" % label)
    for r in rows:
        who = r.get("handle") or r.get("haid") or "?"
        verdict = r.get("verdict") or "-"
        where = r.get("file") or "-"
        age = r.get("age_seconds")
        age_s = ("%ss ago" % age) if age is not None else ""
        sys.stdout.write("%-24s  %-12s  %-28s  %s\n" % (who, verdict, where, age_s))


def main():
    # Resolve the signing seed IN-PROCESS (env > persisted 0600 > auto-bootstrap). When no
    # seed resolves (offline / enroll failed / throttled), degrade cleanly: an empty roster
    # / a no-op beat. The statusline must NEVER break on a virgin, unenrolled checkout.
    seed = resolve_seed()
    if not seed:
        if VERB == "roster":
            render_roster([])
        return 0
    if VERB == "team-auto":
        # ZERO-TOUCH GITHUB TEAM FORMATION. resolve_seed() above already ENROLLED this HAID
        # (REUSING the bootstrap enroll path) so the CP will not fail-close enroll_required.
        # POST /team/auto with the single-use gh proof INSIDE the signed body (the signature
        # covers method+path+body). On {ok, team_id, mode} print "<team_id>\t<mode>\t<project>"
        # to stdout for the bash caller to persist as team.json (no secret). SECURITY: the gh
        # proof lives ONLY in this request body — it is NEVER printed, logged, or written to
        # stdout/stderr; any failure returns 1 (the caller degrades to solo-mint) and NEVER
        # echoes the proof. A non-2xx / missing ok (enroll_required, rate-limit, no route,
        # transport drop) -> 1.
        gh_user = os.environ.get("PRES_GH_USER") or ""
        gh_proof = os.environ.get("PRES_GH_PROOF") or ""
        repo = os.environ.get("PRES_REPO") or ""
        if not (gh_user and gh_proof and repo):
            return 1
        # AT6 KEY POSSESSION: prove this dev HOLDS the private key of HAID before the server binds it
        # (only the key-holder binds their own haid — closes the "admin+known-victim-HAID" griefing
        # vector). Sign the canonical possession assertion — cp_autoteam.possession_message(haid,
        # slug, gh_user, nonce, ts) — with the enrolled seed (resolve_seed() above already ENROLLED
        # this HAID, so the registered pubkey exists to verify against). Built BYTE-IDENTICAL to
        # cp_autoteam.possession_message over the SAME canonical slug (cp_repoteam.repo_slug). The
        # nonce is single-use + ts is signed, so a captured sig can't be replayed for a different bind.
        import cp_repoteam as R  # the SAME slug canonicalizer the server verifies against.
        slug = R.repo_slug(repo) or repo
        nonce = secrets.token_hex(16)
        ts = int(time.time())
        possession = ("\n".join([
            "heimdall-team-auto-possession-v1", HAID, slug, gh_user, nonce, str(ts),
        ])).encode("utf-8")
        sig = K.sign(seed, possession)
        body = json.dumps({
            "repo": repo,
            "gh_user": gh_user,
            "gh_proof": gh_proof,
            "haid": HAID,
            "sig": sig,
            "nonce": nonce,
            "ts": ts,
        }).encode("utf-8")
        status, resp = request("POST", "/team/auto", body, seed)
        if not (200 <= status < 300) or not isinstance(resp, dict) or not resp.get("ok"):
            return 1
        team_id = resp.get("team_id") or ""
        if not team_id:
            return 1
        mode = resp.get("mode") or ""
        project = resp.get("project") or ""
        sys.stdout.write("%s\t%s\t%s\n" % (team_id, mode, project))
        return 0
    if VERB == "beat":
        # nonce + ts ride INSIDE the signed body (the signature covers it) so the server's
        # replay-nonce gate can prove this is a LIVE, first-use beat — a captured beat cannot
        # be replayed (the nonce is single-use within the freshness window). Unforgeable
        # because signed; only replayable, which the gate catches.
        # activity_ts (OPTIONAL): epoch seconds of last real work, from the client activity
        # stamp. The server derives ACTIVE (fresh) vs IDLE (stale/absent) from it. A bare
        # keeper/daemon beat carries the stamp's older mtime (or null) -> the dev reads IDLE.
        _act_raw = os.environ.get("PRES_ACTIVITY_TS") or ""
        try:
            activity_ts = float(_act_raw) if _act_raw else None
        except ValueError:
            activity_ts = None
        body = json.dumps({
            "project": os.environ.get("PRES_PROJECT") or "",
            "handle": os.environ.get("PRES_HANDLE") or None,
            "verdict": os.environ.get("PRES_VERDICT") or None,
            "file": os.environ.get("PRES_FILE") or None,
            # the beating dev's repo-relative git branch (DATA — a teammate's statusline shows a
            # same-repo dev on ANOTHER branch under their name). None outside a git repo / on an
            # old client → the server stores None and the render shows no branch line (back-compat).
            "branch": os.environ.get("PRES_BRANCH") or None,
            "activity_ts": activity_ts,
            "nonce": secrets.token_hex(16),
            "ts": int(time.time()),
        }).encode()
        status, _ = request("POST", "/presence", body, seed)
        # LOUD on a DROPPED/REFUSED beat — the exit-0-no-output that MASKED the invisible-beat bug
        # is gone. A beat that never lands (transport drop -> status 0, or a non-2xx server refusal)
        # is NAMED on stderr so a human running `heimdall-presence beat` sees the failure instead of
        # nothing. stdout stays CLEAN (the statusline reads stdout); the default exit stays 0 so the
        # statusline never breaks on a flaky beat. STRICT (--strict / HMD_PRESENCE_STRICT=1) makes it
        # exit NONZERO so tooling/tests can assert the failure surfaces.
        if not (200 <= status < 300):
            strict = bool(os.environ.get("PRES_STRICT"))
            reason = "unreachable (transport drop)" if status == 0 else ("HTTP %d" % status)
            sys.stderr.write("heimdall presence: beat NOT delivered — %s\n" % reason)
            return 1 if strict else 0
        return 0
    if VERB == "retire":
        # The opt-out prompt-disappearance path: POST /presence-retire so the server writes a
        # retirement tombstone and drops this dev from teammates' rosters on the NEXT read (no
        # 45s TTL wait). Signed with the dev's OWN seed (retire yourself only). Fire-and-forget
        # — if the seed/URL is offline the retire is a no-op and the TTL expiry is the fallback.
        body = json.dumps({
            "project": os.environ.get("PRES_PROJECT") or "",
            "nonce": secrets.token_hex(16),
            "ts": int(time.time()),
        }).encode()
        request("POST", "/presence-retire", body, seed)
        return 0
    if VERB == "roster":
        project = os.environ.get("PRES_PROJECT") or ""
        path = "/roster?" + urllib.parse.urlencode({"project": project})
        st, b = request("GET", path, b"", seed)
        rows = b.get("roster") if isinstance(b, dict) else None
        render_roster(rows if isinstance(rows, list) else [])
        return 0
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main())
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — never traceback; degrade to offline/empty.
        if AS_JSON:
            sys.stdout.write("[]\n")
        elif VERB == "roster":
            sys.stdout.write("presence: no teammates online\n")
        sys.exit(0)
PYEOF
}

# ── FIRST-RUN TEAM RESOLUTION (zero-touch team formation) ──────────────────────────
# On the FIRST wire beat with NO team binding yet, resolve the repo's team ONCE:
#   • a GitHub repo (origin on github.com) + `gh` installed & authed + presence ACTIVE (a URL
#     resolves -> NOT severed) -> POST /team/auto: the FIRST teammate INITIATES the repo's
#     shared team, EVERYONE else on the same repo AUTO-JOINS the SAME team — no invite, no
#     paste. Persist the returned NON-SECRET team_id (source:"auto-github", NO bearer secret —
#     the GitHub proof binds membership server-side; signed beats need no team header).
#   • else (no gh / no GitHub remote / air-gapped / severed / HMD_AUTO_TEAM_DISABLE) -> SOLO-MINT
#     (unchanged), so nothing regresses for non-GitHub / offline use.
# Idempotent (an existing binding short-circuits) + best-effort (any failure -> solo/offline,
# never a crash). Severed is enforced UPSTREAM too: a severed beat has an EMPTY URL and no-ops
# at the offline-degrade gate BEFORE dispatch, so /team/auto is never reached (zero egress).

# owner/repo of a github.com `origin` remote, else empty. GIT-ONLY (no network, no gh).
_github_slug() {
  local url norm
  url="$(git config --get remote.origin.url 2>/dev/null || true)"
  [ -n "$url" ] || return 0
  norm="$(normalize_remote "$url")"   # scheme/userinfo/port/.git stripped, lowercased
  case "$norm" in
    github.com/*/*) printf '%s' "${norm#github.com/}" ;;   # -> owner/repo
    *) return 0 ;;                                          # not github.com -> not a candidate
  esac
}

# SOLO-MINT fallback (the ORIGINAL zero-config behavior): write a fresh 0600 solo team.json and
# set TEAM_SECRET so the enroll/beat below carries it in the X-Heimdall-Team-Secret header. A dev
# starts in their OWN solo team (sees only themselves until they invite). python-side IO (no jq);
# any failure leaves TEAM_SECRET empty (header omitted — graceful).
_solo_mint() {
  # §2 — NEVER auto-solo a GITHUB repo unless /team/auto was already ATTEMPTED-and-failed this
  # session (_AUTO_TEAM_TRIED). Otherwise a github repo would fragment into per-machine solo teams
  # instead of converging on the server repo->team binding (the public-repo explosion). A truly-
  # local tree (no github remote) OR auto explicitly disabled still solo-mints (zero-config in your
  # OWN team). Reached only as the P3-no-secret / P5 fallback from _resolve_team_for_wire.
  if [ -n "$(_github_slug)" ] && [ -z "${HMD_AUTO_TEAM_DISABLE:-}" ] && [ -z "${_AUTO_TEAM_TRIED:-}" ]; then
    return 0
  fi
  TEAM_SECRET="$(HMD_TEAM_DIR_R="$TEAM_DIR" HMD_TEAM_FILE_R="$TEAM_FILE" "$PY" - 2>/dev/null <<'PYEOF' || true
import json, os, secrets, sys, time
team_dir = os.environ["HMD_TEAM_DIR_R"]
path = os.environ["HMD_TEAM_FILE_R"]

def _read(p):
    try:
        s = json.load(open(p)).get("team_secret")
    except Exception:
        return ""
    return s if isinstance(s, str) else ""

try:
    os.makedirs(team_dir, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    sec = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600)
    try:
        os.write(fd, (json.dumps({"team_secret": sec, "created": int(time.time()), "source": "auto-solo"}) + "\n").encode("utf-8"))
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    os.chmod(path, 0o600)
    sys.stdout.write(sec)
except FileExistsError:
    sys.stdout.write(_read(path))   # a concurrent mint won the race -> read it back
except Exception:
    sys.stdout.write("")            # nowhere to persist -> stay header-less
PYEOF
)"
}

# The auto-github attempt. Resolves gh identity + a SINGLE-USE gh token (transit-only), then
# drives the signed enroll + POST /team/auto in-process (REUSE run_client's seed/enroll/signer),
# and persists the returned team_id as team.json (source:"auto-github", NO secret). Returns 0 on
# a bound team (+ an honest one-liner to stderr, interactive only), nonzero on ANY miss (caller
# falls back to solo-mint). gh TOKEN DISCIPLINE: fetched here, passed to run_client via the
# ENVIRONMENT only (PRES_GH_PROOF — never argv, which shows in `ps`), scrubbed from the shell
# immediately after the call, NEVER written to disk and NEVER echoed (even on error).
_auto_team_call() {
  local slug gh_user gh_proof
  slug="$(_github_slug)"; [ -n "$slug" ] || return 1        # not a github.com repo
  command -v gh >/dev/null 2>&1 || return 1                 # gh not installed
  gh_user="$(gh api user --jq .login 2>/dev/null || true)"  # proves gh authed; empty -> bail
  [ -n "$gh_user" ] || return 1
  gh_proof="$(gh auth token 2>/dev/null || true)"           # single-use forward; transit-only
  [ -n "$gh_proof" ] || return 1
  local out
  out="$(PRES_GH_USER="$gh_user" PRES_GH_PROOF="$gh_proof" PRES_REPO="$slug" run_client team-auto 2>/dev/null || true)"
  gh_proof=""; unset gh_proof                                # scrub the proof from the shell ASAP
  [ -n "$out" ] || return 1                                  # no {ok, team_id} -> miss
  local team_id mode
  team_id="$(printf '%s' "$out" | head -1 | cut -f1)"
  mode="$(printf '%s' "$out" | head -1 | cut -f2)"
  [ -n "$team_id" ] || return 1
  # Persist the NON-SECRET team_id (0600; O_EXCL so a concurrent join never clobbers a binding).
  HMD_TEAM_FILE_W="$TEAM_FILE" HMD_TEAM_DIR_W="$TEAM_DIR" HMD_TEAM_ID_W="$team_id" \
    "$PY" - <<'PYEOF' 2>/dev/null || return 1
import json, os, sys, time
d = os.environ["HMD_TEAM_DIR_W"]
p = os.environ["HMD_TEAM_FILE_W"]
tid = os.environ["HMD_TEAM_ID_W"]
try:
    os.makedirs(d, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    # MERGE (not O_EXCL-create): a FRESH repo (no file) -> {team_id, source:auto-github, NO secret};
    # a repo whose team.json ALREADY carries a committed bearer secret -> that secret is PRESERVED
    # (the P4 offline fallback) while we stamp the server team_id as the operative online id. This is
    # the "committed-secret github repo migrates to /team/auto" reconciliation — the split-bug fix.
    # Idempotent: re-stamping the same id rewrites identical content. Two concurrent writers land the
    # SAME server-derived id (deterministic per repo_slug), so the TRUNC race is benign.
    try:
        rec = json.load(open(p))
        if not isinstance(rec, dict):
            rec = {}
    except Exception:
        rec = {}
    rec["team_id"] = tid
    rec.setdefault("source", "auto-github")   # only a first-run (secret-less) file gets auto-github
    rec.setdefault("created", int(time.time()))
    fd = os.open(p, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
    try:
        os.write(fd, (json.dumps(rec) + "\n").encode("utf-8"))
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    os.chmod(p, 0o600)
except Exception:
    sys.exit(1)
PYEOF
  # Honest one-liner — stderr only (stdout is the statusline's), gated to a human at a terminal
  # so the render fork never spams (same discipline as the crypto-missing warning).
  if [ -n "$INTERACTIVE" ]; then
    if [ "$mode" = "initiated" ]; then
      printf 'heimdall: initiated the team for %s (via GitHub)\n' "$PROJECT" >&2
    else
      printf 'heimdall: joined your team for %s (via GitHub)\n' "$PROJECT" >&2
    fi
  fi
  return 0
}

# Resolve the per-repo team for a WIRE beat, ONCE, before the signed enroll/beat. An existing
# binding (a secret in team.json/shared read above, OR an auto-github team.json file) short-
# circuits — idempotent, do nothing new. First run: try zero-touch auto-github, else solo-mint.
# Auto-github is SKIPPED straight to solo when disabled (HMD_AUTO_TEAM_DISABLE), when presence is
# severed/offline (empty URL -> no /team/auto egress), or with no signer/identity/project.
# team.json already carries a server team_id (P1)? Mirrors heimdall-team:team_has_auto_id — a
# github binding short-circuits (idempotent, no /team/auto re-POST, no header).
_team_file_has_id() {
  [ -f "$TEAM_FILE" ] || return 1
  HMD_TEAM_FILE_R="$TEAM_FILE" "$PY" - <<'PYEOF' 2>/dev/null
import json, os, sys
try:
    d = json.load(open(os.environ["HMD_TEAM_FILE_R"]))
    sys.exit(0 if isinstance(d, dict) and isinstance(d.get("team_id"), str) and d.get("team_id") else 1)
except Exception:
    sys.exit(1)
PYEOF
}

_resolve_team_for_wire() {
  [ -n "$PY" ] || return 0
  # P1 — team.json already carries a server team_id (auto-github, OR a MIGRATED committed file):
  # the server repo->team binding IS membership. Drop any header + short-circuit (idempotent).
  if _team_file_has_id; then TEAM_SECRET=""; return 0; fi
  # P2 — a GITHUB repo, online (URL resolves -> not severed), auto not disabled: /team/auto is THE
  # authority. Prefer it EVEN when a committed/legacy secret is present — THAT is the split-bug fix
  # (the old code returned on a non-empty secret BEFORE ever calling /team/auto, so the secret
  # header re-bound the HAID to sha256(secret) and split the repo). On success DROP the header +
  # persist the server team_id (merged into team.json, secret preserved for offline).
  local _slug; _slug="$(_github_slug)"
  if [ -n "$_slug" ] && [ -z "${HMD_AUTO_TEAM_DISABLE:-}" ] && [ -n "$URL" ] && [ -n "$HAID" ] && [ -n "$PROJECT" ]; then
    _AUTO_TEAM_TRIED=1
    if _auto_team_call; then TEAM_SECRET=""; return 0; fi
  fi
  # P3/P4 — /team/auto deferred/denied (no gh auth / non-collaborator / rate-limit) or offline: a
  # committed/legacy/solo secret rides in the header (online fallback) / is retained locally
  # (offline, self-heals to P2 on reconnect). Non-empty -> done.
  [ -n "$TEAM_SECRET" ] && return 0
  # P5 / P3-no-secret — no github remote (truly local), OR github+auto-tried-and-failed with no
  # secret: solo-mint so a dev is never teamless (gated: never a fresh solo for an untried github repo).
  _solo_mint
}

# Best-effort ONE final signed retire beat (opt-out prompt-disappearance). Only attempts when
# the wire is resolvable (URL+HAID+PROJECT+signer present); otherwise the TTL expiry is the
# graceful fallback. Never fatal — an offline `off` still writes the local toggle.
_try_retire() {
  [ -n "$PY" ] || return 0
  [ -f "$LIB/cp_auth.py" ] || return 0
  [ -n "$URL" ] && [ -n "$HAID" ] && [ -n "$PROJECT" ] || return 0
  run_client retire >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}

# ── DURABLE PRESENCE KEEPER ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A detached loop that re-beats on a timer so a LIVE-BUT-IDLE session (no statusline
# renders, no manual beats) stays on the wall instead of ageing out past the ~45s TTL.
# It REUSES `beat` for every heartbeat (its consent gate no-ops an off beat too) — it
# NEVER re-implements beating. The keeper is keyed per (project, session): its pid lives
# in ONE file under the runtime home so keeper-stop reaps exactly the loop this session
# started, and a stale-pid guard + a wallclock backstop mean a crashed session never
# orphans a loop forever. Everything is best-effort + silent-safe: a keeper fault (offline,
# CP down, no place to persist) never breaks the session.

# runtime keeper dir (under the runtime home; overridable for tests — never hardcoded).
_keeper_dir() { printf '%s' "${HEIMDALL_KEEPER_DIR:-$HMD_DIR/presence-keeper}"; }
# session key: --session > $HMD_SESSION_ID > $CLAUDE_SESSION_ID > "default" (repo-scoped).
_keeper_session() {
  local s="$SESSION"
  [ -n "$s" ] || s="${HMD_SESSION_ID:-}"
  [ -n "$s" ] || s="${CLAUDE_SESSION_ID:-}"
  [ -n "$s" ] || s="default"
  printf '%s' "$s"
}
# the per-(project,session) pidfile. Slugs '/:@ ' so a remote-derived project id + a session
# id never break the filename.
_keeper_pidfile() {
  [ -n "$KEEPER_PIDFILE" ] && { printf '%s' "$KEEPER_PIDFILE"; return; }
  local proj sess
  proj="$(printf '%s' "${PROJECT:-repo}" | tr '/:@ ' '____')"
  sess="$(printf '%s' "$(_keeper_session)" | tr '/:@ ' '____')"
  printf '%s/%s__%s.pid' "$(_keeper_dir)" "$proj" "$sess"
}
# is a LIVE keeper recorded in $1? (pidfile present, numeric pid, process alive).
_keeper_alive() {
  local pf="$1" pid
  [ -f "$pf" ] || return 1
  pid="$(cat "$pf" 2>/dev/null || true)"
  case "$pid" in ''|*[!0-9]*) return 1 ;; esac
  kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null
}

# The loop itself. Claims the pidfile with its OWN pid, then beats every INTERVAL until it is
# killed, its pidfile stops naming it (soft-stop / a newer keeper won the file), it hits the
# cycle cap (a test seam), or it exceeds the wallclock backstop (orphan guard). Reaps its own
# pidfile on exit. TERM/INT are trapped so keeper-stop kills it PROMPTLY (the in-flight sleep
# is interrupted + reaped, so no zombie sleep is left behind).
_keeper_loop() {
  local pidfile="$1" interval="$2"
  local beat_bin="${HMD_KEEPER_BEAT_BIN:-$SELF}"      # test seam: inject a recording beat stub.
  local max_cycles="${HMD_KEEPER_MAX_CYCLES:-0}"      # 0 = unbounded (a positive N = test seam).
  local max_seconds="${HMD_KEEPER_MAX_SECONDS:-86400}" # 24h orphan backstop (0 = unbounded).
  local start_ts now cycles=0 swait=""
  start_ts="$(date +%s 2>/dev/null || echo 0)"
  mkdir -p "$(dirname "$pidfile")" 2>/dev/null || true
  # claim ownership atomically (last writer wins; the loser sees the mismatch + exits below).
  printf '%s\n' "$$" > "$pidfile.tmp.$$" 2>/dev/null && mv -f "$pidfile.tmp.$$" "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null
  # shellcheck disable=SC2064 — expand $pidfile/$swait/$$ at trap-fire time, not define time.
  trap 'rm -f "$pidfile.tmp.$$" 2>/dev/null; [ -n "$swait" ] && kill "$swait" 2>/dev/null; [ "$(cat "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null)" = "$$" ] && rm -f "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null; exit 0' TERM INT
  while :; do
    "$beat_bin" beat >/dev/null 2>&1 || true          # REUSE beat (its consent gate applies).
    # Refresh the statusline's ledger status.json on the SAME beat cadence (HMD Statusline
    # Spec v1 §6) so the file the statusline reads stays warm while the session is live. This
    # is where the daemon "watching" liveness comes from — the keeper's own pidfile. Best-effort
    # + silent: a status-write fault NEVER perturbs the heartbeat. Skipped under the beat-injection
    # test seam so the keeper falsifier stays hermetic (no real status-source reads / no ~/.heimdall
    # writes in tests).
    if [ -z "${HMD_KEEPER_BEAT_BIN:-}" ] && [ -x "$SELF_DIR/heimdall-status-json" ]; then
      "$SELF_DIR/heimdall-status-json" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
    fi
    cycles=$((cycles + 1))
    # THROTTLED RESOURCE GC: every N beats fire a cheap, backgrounded `heimdall-gc run
    # --quick` so a LONG-LIVED session keeps freeing temp files + stale pidfiles
    # "constantly" (not just at session end). CHEAP (quick = temp + orphan pidfiles,
    # skips the git worktree pass) + THROTTLED (default every 30 beats ≈ 10min at the
    # 20s interval) + backgrounded + best-effort. SKIPPED under the beat-injection test
    # seam (HMD_KEEPER_BEAT_BIN) so hermetic keeper tests never shell out to gc.
    if [ -z "${HMD_KEEPER_BEAT_BIN:-}" ]; then
      local gc_every="${HMD_GC_KEEPER_BEATS:-30}"
      case "$gc_every" in ''|*[!0-9]*) gc_every=0 ;; esac
      if [ "$gc_every" -gt 0 ] && [ "$((cycles % gc_every))" -eq 0 ]; then
        local gc_bin="$SELF_DIR/heimdall-gc"
        [ -x "$gc_bin" ] && ( "$gc_bin" run --quick --quiet >/dev/null 2>&1 & ) || true
      fi
    fi
    [ "$max_cycles" != "0" ] && [ "$cycles" -ge "$max_cycles" ] && break
    # soft-stop / stale-pid guard: if the pidfile no longer names us, a stop (rm) or a newer
    # keeper claimed it -> exit so there is ever only ONE live keeper per session.
    [ "$(cat "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null || true)" = "$$" ] || break
    now="$(date +%s 2>/dev/null || echo 0)"           # wallclock backstop against an orphan.
    [ "$max_seconds" != "0" ] && [ "$((now - start_ts))" -ge "$max_seconds" ] && break
    sleep "$interval" & swait=$!; wait "$swait" 2>/dev/null; swait=""
  done
  [ "$(cat "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null || true)" = "$$" ] && rm -f "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null || true
  return 0
}

# _sandbox_home — true when $HOME resolves under an OS temp root ($TMPDIR, /tmp, /var/tmp,
# their macOS /private/* real paths, and macOS's per-user Darwin temp root — mktemp -d's own
# territory). EXISTS BECAUSE: a hermetic install (`env -i HOME="$(mktemp -d)" ... install.sh`)
# reaches the doctor auto-launch below through a REAL SessionStart hook fired by
# heimdall-doctor-install's headless `claude --cc-verify` probe (install.sh §5a) — a genuine,
# correct hook firing, NOT a test stubbing keeper-start directly. `env -i` wipes every env var
# the harness does not explicitly re-list, so the usual test-only escape hatch (a NEW env-var
# seam) can never reach this deep without editing that harness's allowlist — confirmed
# empty-handed (the cc-verify probe itself sets no marker either). $HOME is therefore the only
# signal left standing: the harness MUST set it for the sandbox to mean anything at all, so
# unlike an added env var it can never simply go missing.
#
# CAUGHT LIVE (test/install-stranger.test.sh's real run_install(), post-first-fix): `env -i`
# ALSO wipes $TMPDIR, and on macOS `mktemp -d` roots its output under the per-user Darwin temp
# dir (/var/folders/<xx>/<hash>/T/tmp.XXXXXXXX) — a path that is neither /tmp nor /var/tmp, so
# with $TMPDIR gone the plain path list above never recognizes it and the guard silently does
# not fire for exactly the real trigger it exists to catch (confirmed: a real install-stranger
# run leaked 2 live doctors after the first fix landed). `getconf DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR` reads
# that same root via confstr(3) — keyed off the real uid, not an env lookup — so it survives
# `env -i` intact and needs no cooperation from the wiped environment. Harmless elsewhere:
# non-macOS (or a stripped-down PATH missing `getconf`) just yields an empty candidate, which
# the loop below already skips.
_sandbox_home() {
  [ -n "${HOME:-}" ] || return 1
  local h rt t darwin_tmp
  h="$(cd "$HOME" 2>/dev/null && pwd -P)" || h="$HOME"
  darwin_tmp="$(command -v getconf >/dev/null 2>&1 && getconf DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR 2>/dev/null)"
  for t in "${TMPDIR:-}" /tmp /var/tmp /private/tmp /private/var/tmp "$darwin_tmp"; do
    [ -n "$t" ] || continue
    t="${t%/}"
    rt="$(cd "$t" 2>/dev/null && pwd -P)" || rt="$t"
    [ -n "$rt" ] || continue
    case "$h" in "$rt"|"$rt"/*) return 0 ;; esac
  done
  return 1
}

# keeper-start: consent-gated, idempotent, detached spawn of ONE keeper for this session.
_keeper_start() {
  # CONSENT OFF -> NO keeper. Mirror `off`: a best-effort retire so we are not on the wall,
  # then return. (The loop's beats would no-op anyway, but not spawning it is the honest
  # "consent off -> no keeper" contract and wastes no process.)
  if _pres_off; then _try_retire; printf 'presence keeper: not started (presence is OFF)\n'; return 0; fi
  # NOT CONNECTED -> NO keeper (and NO doctor). With no resolved URL the dev has not opted in
  # to the control plane (undecided/declined, no env/config override); spawning a keeper +
  # the autoenroll doctor would waste a process (both no-op at their own URL gate anyway).
  # Fail-safe: don't. `hmd presence connect` resolves a URL and a later keeper-start arms it.
  # EXEMPTION: an explicit beat-injection seam (HMD_KEEPER_BEAT_BIN) drives its OWN beat
  # mechanism (tooling/tests), so it owns the decision — the URL gate does not apply there.
  if [ -z "$URL" ] && [ -z "${HMD_KEEPER_BEAT_BIN:-}" ]; then
    printf 'presence keeper: not started (control plane not connected — run: hmd presence connect)\n'
    return 0
  fi
  local pidfile interval i=0
  pidfile="$(_keeper_pidfile)"
  interval="${INTERVAL:-${HMD_KEEPER_INTERVAL:-20}}"
  mkdir -p "$(_keeper_dir)" 2>/dev/null || true
  if _keeper_alive "$pidfile"; then
    printf 'presence keeper: already running (pid %s) — not spawning a second\n' "$(cat "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null)"
    return 0
  fi
  rm -f "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null || true               # reap a stale pidfile (dead pid).
  # Detach: RE-EXEC this bin as a fresh `keeper-loop` process (NOT a subshell of us) so the loop
  # runs as its OWN top-level shell — `$$` inside is then its real pid (a subshell's $$ is the
  # PARENT's, and $BASHPID is bash-4-only, absent on macOS's stock bash 3.2). nohup + disown +
  # </dev/null detach it from this hook/shell so it survives the session; the loop self-claims
  # the pidfile with its own $$.
  nohup "$SELF" keeper-loop --pidfile "$pidfile" --interval "$interval" </dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1 &
  disown 2>/dev/null || true
  # Briefly wait for the loop to claim the pidfile so an immediate double-start sees it (closes
  # the idempotency race). Best-effort — the keeper is armed regardless of this confirmation.
  while [ "$i" -lt 40 ]; do _keeper_alive "$pidfile" && break; i=$((i + 1)); sleep 0.05 2>/dev/null || sleep 1; done
  if _keeper_alive "$pidfile"; then
    printf 'presence keeper: started (pid %s, beats every %ss)\n' "$(cat "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null)" "$interval"
  else
    printf 'presence keeper: could not confirm start (best-effort — presence still beats on render)\n'
  fi
  # SELF-HEALING AUTOENROLL: launch the background presence-doctor (detached, idempotent,
  # consent-gated) alongside the keeper — it diagnoses+remediates+verifies (crypto backend,
  # interpreter, stale throttle, enroll, roster) until presence is HEALTHY, then quiesces.
  # REUSES this already-SessionStart-wired keeper-start path (no new hooks.json edit). The
  # doctor is its OWN detached process (nohup+disown) so it outlives + runs independent of the
  # keeper loop. SKIPPED under the keeper's beat-injection test seam (HMD_KEEPER_BEAT_BIN), an
  # explicit HMD_DOCTOR_DISABLE, and (below) a sandbox-shaped $HOME — so hermetic tests never
  # trigger the doctor's real network AND a throwaway sandbox HOME never gets a detached
  # process that outlives the very directory it was born in.
  DOCTOR_BIN="$SELF_DIR/heimdall-presence-doctor"
  if [ -x "$DOCTOR_BIN" ] && [ -z "${HMD_KEEPER_BEAT_BIN:-}" ] && [ -z "${HMD_DOCTOR_DISABLE:-}" ]; then
    # SANDBOX GUARD: $HOME under a temp root (mktemp -d) means something is going to rm -rf it
    # the moment ITS OWN run ends — a hermetic install harness, most commonly (see
    # test/install-stranger.test.sh -> install.sh §5a -> heimdall-doctor-install --cc-verify ->
    # the real SessionStart hook -> here). A detached doctor (up to HMD_DOCTOR_MAX_SECONDS,
    # default 1800s) has no way to know that on its own, so it outlives its own HOME and
    # orphans. Observable on purpose (not a silent no-op) — it can only ever print in this one
    # narrow case, since a real dev's $HOME is never rooted under a temp dir.
    if _sandbox_home; then
      printf 'presence keeper: self-heal doctor NOT auto-launched (HOME=%s is a sandbox temp dir)\n' "$HOME"
    else
      nohup "$DOCTOR_BIN" --bg </dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1 &
      disown 2>/dev/null || true
    fi
  fi
  return 0
}

# keeper-stop: kill THIS session's keeper + reap its pidfile. Idempotent (a missing/stale/dead
# keeper is a clean no-op). Sends TERM, escalates to KILL if it lingers, then removes the file.
_keeper_stop() {
  local pidfile pid i=0
  pidfile="$(_keeper_pidfile)"
  [ -f "$pidfile" ] || { printf 'presence keeper: not running\n'; return 0; }
  pid="$(cat "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null || true)"
  case "$pid" in
    ''|*[!0-9]*) rm -f "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null || true; printf 'presence keeper: stale pidfile cleared\n'; return 0 ;;
  esac
  if kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null; then
    kill "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true
    while [ "$i" -lt 20 ] && kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null; do i=$((i + 1)); sleep 0.05 2>/dev/null || sleep 1; done
    kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null && kill -9 "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true
    printf 'presence keeper: stopped (pid %s)\n' "$pid"
  else
    printf 'presence keeper: already gone (pid %s)\n' "$pid"
  fi
  rm -f "$pidfile" 2>/dev/null || true
  return 0
}

case "$SUB" in
  beat)
    # Effectively-on here (the OFF guard above already no-op'd an off beat). Honor the
    # --no-files sub-toggle: withhold the file field so the beat body sends file:null.
    _repo_nofiles && FILE=""
    # FIRST-RUN TEAM: with no binding yet, form the repo's team zero-touch (auto-github, else
    # solo-mint) BEFORE the signed enroll/beat, so the enroll lands in the right team. Idempotent
    # + best-effort; a severed beat never reaches here (it no-ops at the offline-degrade gate).
    _resolve_team_for_wire
    # Resolve the wall-state activity signal: an ACTIVE-verdict beat bumps the stamp to now, a
    # bare keeper/daemon beat carries the stamp mtime forward, absent -> null (server -> IDLE).
    ACTIVITY_TS="$(_resolve_activity_ts)"
    # the repo-relative branch this beat rides → teammates see a same-repo dev on another branch.
    BRANCH="$(_resolve_branch)"
    run_client beat ;;
  activity)
    # BUMP the activity stamp to now — the edit hook's entry point ("real work happened").
    # Local, consent-independent (a pure mtime, no beat, no network); the NEXT beat reads it.
    _bump_activity_stamp ;;
  activity-ts)
    # Print the activity_ts the next beat WOULD send (HMD_ACTIVITY_TS > active-verdict-now >
    # stamp mtime > empty). A debug + test seam; honors HMD_VERDICT exactly as `beat` does.
    _resolve_activity_ts; printf '\n' ;;
  keeper-start) _keeper_start ;;
  keeper-stop)  _keeper_stop ;;
  keeper-loop)  # INTERNAL: run one keeper loop in-process. Used by keeper-start's detached
                # spawn and by the falsifier test to drive N deterministic cycles.
    _keeper_loop "$(_keeper_pidfile)" "${INTERVAL:-${HMD_KEEPER_INTERVAL:-20}}" ;;
  roster) run_client roster ;;   # OFF = invisible, NOT blind: an opted-out dev still SEES the wall.
  retire) run_client retire ;;   # emit ONE signed retire beat (used by `off`; exposed for tooling).
  connect)
    # OPT IN to the live control plane (the affirmative decision). Persist {connected, url}
    # so THIS and every future session auto-resolves the URL with zero re-prompt, then state
    # exactly what is shared (privacy) and send a first beat so the dev appears immediately.
    # --url overrides the canonical default (a self-hosted CP). Reversible: `sever`.
    CU="${URL:-$DEFAULT_CP_URL}"
    if [ -z "$CU" ]; then
      echo "presence connect: no control-plane URL available (canonical default missing and no --url given)" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    if _write_cp_consent "$(printf '{"decision": "connected", "url": "%s", "ts": %s}' "$CU" "$(date +%s 2>/dev/null || echo 0)")"; then
      printf 'presence: CONNECTED to the live control plane\n'
      printf '  url:     %s\n' "$CU"
      printf '  shared with your team (holders of this repo team secret): your HAID, online\n'
      printf '           status, and edit activity (current filename + verdict) — never file contents.\n'
      printf '  future sessions auto-connect (no re-prompt). Reversible: hmd presence sever\n'
      # Best-effort first beat — a fresh sub-invocation re-resolves the URL from the consent
      # we just wrote, so the dev shows up now (silent-safe; offline just no-ops).
      # HMD_CP_CONNECT_NO_BEAT skips it (hermetic tests assert persistence without a live beat).
      [ -n "${HMD_CP_CONNECT_NO_BEAT:-}" ] || "$SELF" beat >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
    else
      echo "presence connect: could not persist the consent decision ($(_cp_consent_file))" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    ;;
  sever|disconnect)
    # SEVER the Bifröst — the true-zero-egress opt-out (persisted {"decision":"severed"}). Retire
    # from teammates' walls NOW (best-effort — uses the URL still resolved from the prior consent),
    # then persist the sever so the CP URL stops resolving: NO beat, NO roster, NO enroll — nothing
    # leaves this machine — and NEVER re-prompted. Re-enable with `connect`. `disconnect` is a
    # hidden back-compat alias of `sever` (identical effect + persisted state).
    _try_retire
    if _write_cp_consent '{"decision": "severed"}'; then
      printf 'presence: SEVERED from the control plane — local-only. ZERO egress: no beat, no roster, no enroll leaves this machine.\n'
      printf '  you will not be prompted again. Re-enable anytime: hmd presence connect\n'
    else
      echo "presence sever: could not persist the consent decision ($(_cp_consent_file))" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    ;;
  cp-status)
    # INSPECT the control-plane opt-in decision + the URL presence would use (reversible +
    # inspectable). Distinct from `status` (the per-repo visibility toggle): this is the
    # phone-home gate. No secrets are printed.
    D="$(_cp_consent_decision)"; [ -n "$D" ] || D="undecided"
    printf 'presence control-plane connection\n'
    printf '  decision:  %s (%s)\n' "$D" "$(_cp_consent_file)"
    if [ -n "$URL" ]; then
      printf '  url:       %s\n' "$URL"
    else
      printf '  url:       (none — presence is LOCAL/offline; not contacting the control plane)\n'
    fi
    case "$D" in
      connected)      printf '  effect:    ON — presence beats to the control plane (your team can see you). Reversible: hmd presence sever\n' ;;
      severed|declined) printf '  effect:    OFF — severed; ZERO egress, no beat/roster/enroll leaves this machine. Re-enable: hmd presence connect\n' ;;
      *)         if [ -n "$URL" ]; then
                   printf '  effect:    ON — default on (undecided). Opt out: hmd presence sever (disables team/cloud)\n'
                 else
                   printf '  effect:    OFF — no control-plane URL resolves (severed or offline).\n'
                 fi ;;
    esac
    ;;
  connect-prompt)
    # The ONE-TIME opt-OUT disclosure (wired into SessionStart). NEVER blocks a session.
    # Presence is ON BY DEFAULT; this only DISCLOSES that and offers the opt-out.
    #   • already decided (connected/severed/declined) -> respect it, exit silent (no re-prompt).
    #   • an explicit URL override already resolves  -> honored as consent, exit silent.
    #   • UNDECIDED + a real TTY (or HMD_CP_PROMPT_FORCE) -> [Y = keep on / n = disable]; n ->
    #     sever (persist the opt-out), anything else -> connect (pin the opt-in).
    #   • UNDECIDED + non-interactive -> stays ON (DEFAULT) + a throttled one-line opt-out
    #     notice; persist NOTHING so a later interactive session can still pin a decision.
    D="$(_cp_consent_decision)"
    if [ -n "$D" ]; then exit 0; fi
    # An EXPLICIT url override (env / cp-endpoint.json) is itself consent -> stay silent (never
    # nag a power-user who already pointed presence somewhere). NOTE: with DEFAULT ON, $URL is
    # now non-empty for UNDECIDED too (the baked-in CP resolves), so we test the OVERRIDE
    # sources directly — testing $URL would wrongly swallow the first-run opt-out notice.
    if [ -n "${HEIMDALL_CP_URL:-}" ] || [ -n "${BASE_URL:-}" ] || [ -n "$CFG_URL" ]; then exit 0; fi
    if { [ -t 0 ] && [ -t 1 ]; } || [ -n "${HMD_CP_PROMPT_FORCE:-}" ]; then
      printf 'Keep Heimdall presence ON? It shares your HAID, online status, and edit activity\n' >&2
      printf '(current filename + verdict) with your team (holders of this repo team secret) —\n' >&2
      printf 'never file contents.\n' >&2
      printf '[Y = keep on / n = disable] ' >&2
      _ans=""; IFS= read -r _ans 2>/dev/null || _ans=""
      case "$_ans" in
        n|N|no|NO|No) exec "$SELF" sever ;;
        *) exec "$SELF" connect ;;
      esac
    fi
    if _cp_hint_throttled; then
      printf '[heimdall] presence is ON — your online status + edits (filename + verdict, never file contents) are shared with your team. hmd presence sever — disables team/cloud.\n'
    fi
    exit 0
    ;;
  off)
    if [ -n "$GLOBAL" ]; then
      mkdir -p "$HMD_DIR" 2>/dev/null || true
      : > "$GLOBAL_OFF_FILE" 2>/dev/null || true
      printf 'presence: OFF globally (machine-wide kill switch) — %s\n' "$GLOBAL_OFF_FILE"
    else
      _write_pres_state '{"enabled": false}'
      printf 'presence: OFF for this repo — %s\n' "$PRES_STATE_FILE"
    fi
    # Retire NOW so you drop from teammates' walls promptly (no 45s TTL wait).
    _try_retire
    printf 'you can still SEE the team; the team can no longer see you. (hmd presence on to return)\n'
    ;;
  on)
    if [ -n "$GLOBAL" ]; then
      rm -f "$GLOBAL_OFF_FILE" 2>/dev/null || true
      printf 'presence: ON globally — %s removed\n' "$GLOBAL_OFF_FILE"
    fi
    if [ -n "$NOFILES" ]; then
      _write_pres_state '{"enabled": true, "files": false}'
      printf 'presence: ON for this repo, file detail WITHHELD (--no-files) — handle+verdict only\n'
    elif [ -z "$GLOBAL" ]; then
      _write_pres_state '{"enabled": true}'
      printf 'presence: ON for this repo — %s\n' "$PRES_STATE_FILE"
    fi
    ;;
  status)
    _global_pres_off && G="off" || G="on"
    _repo_pres_off   && R="off" || R="on"
    _repo_nofiles    && FILES="withheld (--no-files)" || FILES="shown"
    if _pres_off; then
      EFF="OFF"
      if _global_pres_off; then WHY="global kill switch is on"; else WHY="this repo is opted out"; fi
    else
      EFF="ON"; WHY="broadcasting handle + verdict$([ "$FILES" = shown ] && printf ' + current file')"
    fi
    SIGN="$(_signing_probe)"
    printf 'presence status\n'
    printf '  repo:      %-4s (%s)\n' "$R" "$PRES_STATE_FILE"
    printf '  global:    %-4s (%s)\n' "$G" "$GLOBAL_OFF_FILE"
    printf '  effective: %s — %s\n' "$EFF" "$WHY"
    printf '  files:     %s\n' "$FILES"
    # The signing-backend line REVEALS the crypto gap: presence can be effective:ON yet
    # SILENTLY DISABLED when the Ed25519 backend is missing (no seed → every beat dropped).
    case "$SIGN" in
      ok:*)    printf '  signing:   Ed25519 backend OK (%s)\n' "${SIGN#ok:}" ;;
      missing) printf '  signing:   MISSING — presence disabled, run %s -m pip install --user cryptography\n' "${PY:-python3}" ;;
      *)       printf '  signing:   unknown (could not probe the Ed25519 backend)\n' ;;
    esac
    # The self-heal doctor's LAST DIAGNOSIS (if it has run) — surfaces WHY presence is/isn't
    # healthy in the natural place a dev checks. `heimdall-presence doctor` heals it in the bg.
    if [ -n "$DOCTOR_DIAG" ] && [ -f "$DOCTOR_DIAG" ] && [ -n "$PY" ]; then
      DIAG_LINE="$("$PY" - "$DOCTOR_DIAG" 2>/dev/null <<'PYEOF' || true
import json, sys
try:
    d = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))
    st = d.get("state") or "?"
    msg = d.get("reason") or ""
    sys.stdout.write("%s%s" % (st, (" — %s" % msg) if msg else ""))
except Exception:
    sys.stdout.write("")
PYEOF
)"
      [ -n "$DIAG_LINE" ] && printf '  doctor:    %s\n' "$DIAG_LINE"
    fi
    printf '  note: OFF = invisible, not blind — you can still SEE the team; the team cannot see you.\n'
    ;;
  ""|-h|--help|help)
    cat <<'USAGE'
heimdall-presence — server-synced team presence (with consent opt-out)

  heimdall-presence connect [--url U] OPT IN to the live control plane: persist the decision +
                                      URL so every future session auto-connects (no re-prompt),
                                      state what is shared, and beat once so you appear now.
  heimdall-presence sever             OPT OUT (true zero egress): retire now + empty the CP URL so
                                      NO beat/roster/enroll leaves this machine (never re-prompted).
                                      Presence stays LOCAL. Re-enable with connect.
  heimdall-presence cp-status         print the control-plane opt-in decision + resolved URL.
  heimdall-presence beat              send a heartbeat for this repo's project + identity
  heimdall-presence roster [--json]   print the online team for this repo's project
  heimdall-presence off               stop broadcasting from THIS repo (+ retire now)
  heimdall-presence on  [--no-files]  re-enable this repo (--no-files: withhold file detail)
  heimdall-presence off --global      machine-wide kill switch (~/.heimdall/presence-off)
  heimdall-presence on  --global      lift the machine-wide kill switch
  heimdall-presence status            print repo/global/effective state + what is broadcast
  heimdall-presence retire            emit one signed retire beat (drop off walls now)
  heimdall-presence keeper-start [--session ID] [--interval S]
                                      spawn ONE detached background beat-keeper (default 20s,
                                      under the ~45s TTL) so a LIVE-BUT-IDLE session stays on
                                      the wall. Idempotent + consent-gated + silent-safe.
  heimdall-presence keeper-stop  [--session ID]
                                      kill this session's keeper + reap its pidfile (no leak)
  heimdall-presence doctor            SELF-HEAL: diagnose+remediate+verify autoenroll once
  heimdall-presence doctor --bg       detached background self-heal loop (keeper-start runs it)
  heimdall-presence doctor --status   print the self-heal doctor's last diagnosis

KEEPER (durable presence): a single SessionStart beat ages out past the TTL and the statusline
beat only fires on a REDRAW — so a live-but-idle session vanishes from the wall. keeper-start
runs a detached loop that re-beats on a timer (reusing `beat` + its consent gate) until
keeper-stop reaps it at SessionEnd. The pid lives in ONE file under the runtime home
(~/.heimdall/presence-keeper/<project>__<session>.pid, or $HEIMDALL_KEEPER_DIR); a stale-pid
guard + a 24h wallclock backstop mean a crashed session never orphans a loop. OFF -> no keeper.

DEV-CHECKOUT (heimdall on PATH but NOT a registered plugin -> the plugin's SessionStart hook
never fires): wire the two subcommands into your OWN ~/.claude/settings.json so the keeper still
starts/stops with your session (paths resolve dynamically — no hardcoding):
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command",
      "command": "SID=$(jq -r '.session_id // empty'); heimdall-presence keeper-start --session \"$SID\" >/dev/null 2>&1 &"}]}],
    "SessionEnd":   [{"hooks": [{"type": "command",
      "command": "SID=$(jq -r '.session_id // empty'); heimdall-presence keeper-stop  --session \"$SID\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true"}]}]
  }
Or just run install.sh, which registers the plugin whose shipped hooks call them for you.

OPT-OUT (DEFAULT ON): presence contacts the live control plane BY DEFAULT — an undecided or
`connect`ed dev resolves the baked-in CP URL and beats. Opt out with `sever`: it persists the
opt-out so NO URL resolves, every beat is a no-op, roster degrades to empty WITHOUT a wire
call, and NOTHING leaves this machine (zero egress). `connect` pins the opt-in +{url} to
~/.heimdall/cp-consent.json (0600); `cp-status` shows the current decision + URL. On session
start an UNDECIDED dev sees the opt-out disclosure ONCE (connect-prompt): a TTY gets a
[Y = keep on / n = disable] choice, a non-interactive session prints a single throttled one-line
notice and stays ON. An explicit --url / $HEIMDALL_CP_URL / cp-endpoint.json is honored as-is.
The consent decision is per-USER (~/.heimdall); the visibility toggles below (on/off/--no-files)
are per-REPO and layer on top.

CONSENT: OFF = zero beats (a stat-only no-op — a cron/hook can't leak around it) AND a retire
beat so you vanish from teammates' walls promptly, not after the TTL. OFF is invisible, NOT
blind: `roster` still shows the team. Broadcast is ONLY handle + verdict + current filename —
never file contents, never code. --no-files keeps you present but sends file:null.

ZERO-CONFIG (once connected): the first beat/roster auto-resolves the url (the canonical
default, or your --url/config), auto-generates+enrolls+persists a 0600 signing key, derives a
stable project id from the git remote, and reads the handle from heimdall-identity — the
dev exports NOTHING. Overrides still win:
  Overrides: --haid --project --url --handle --verdict --file --global --no-files
  Env: HMD_HAID HMD_PROJECT HMD_HANDLE HMD_VERDICT HMD_FILE HMD_ENROLL_THROTTLE
       HEIMDALL_PRESENCE_DIR (per-repo state dir override)
       HEIMDALL_CP_URL|BASE_URL  HMD_PRESENCE_SEED (dev key override; server's HEIMDALL_CP_PKI_KEY is NOT read)
Offline/unconfigured degrades cleanly (empty roster, no-op beat, exit 0).
USAGE
    ;;
  *) echo "heimdall-presence: unknown subcommand '$SUB' (try: connect | sever | cp-status | beat | roster | on | off | status | retire | activity | doctor | keeper-start | keeper-stop)" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
